-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. ROYALTY (REQUIRED FOR COMMERCIAL USE)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
For any Commercial Use, You must pay the Licensor the Royalty Rate on all
Gross Revenue attributable to the Software. Royalties:

  (a) accrue from the first unit of Gross Revenue above the Free Threshold;
  (b) are payable monthly, within fifteen (15) days of each calendar month's
      end, in USDC to codingsh.eth (ENS) on a network supported by the x402
      protocol, OR as otherwise agreed in writing;
  (c) must be accompanied by a reasonable statement of the Gross Revenue on
      which the royalty was computed; and
  (d) are non-refundable.

The Licensor (or its agent) may, no more than once per year and on reasonable
notice, audit records relevant to royalty computation. Underpayment of more
than five percent (5%) for any period entitles the Licensor to recover the
reasonable cost of the audit.

Non-Commercial Use is royalty-free (attribution still required).

